:"2021-03-12T16:40:41-08:00","id":1439537,"title":"","content":"Not every Virtual Adept is going to want to get on the crypto bandwagon. And the VAs have always had relatively easy access to money if they want, and there's a risk as noted of being noticed for being rich.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T16:47:06-08:00","id":1439542,"title":"","content":"Also, do consider the fact that there are VA's who are still using their ancient mainframe's from the 70s and curse these newfangled kids and their silly money, when you have calculated all the points of time and space and your punchcard programmed warehouse is finally working just right. VA's are much more than just the leetkids doing the current newness. There are bound to be hackers that still believe in hacking the Gibson and who don't move away from their CRT monitors and olschool mechanical keyboards. And with magic removing the limitations of your hardware, who's to stop you from being right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T17:13:04-08:00","id":1439546,"title":"","content":"Mages can get money by some means or other if they want or need it. Many Mages would embrace poverty as an aid to spirituality. Not my point of view, but common among mystics. Many Mages live way far off the grid. A Hermetic and a Son of Ether (a charming pair of guys) living in one of the more rural areas of Northern California might produce everything they need. And it's all coincidental. A Cultist in the Oakland area uses their magic to find enough comics and collectables to finance their lifestyle. Because they dress down and rarely visit the same dealer more than twice a year if that it's all coincidental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T10:45:46-08:00","id":1473479,"title":"","content":"Since the Data sphere has always allowed them to do whatever they wanted with bank accounts, I doubt there's any significant shift for them in the area of financial resources. I'd expect the Tradition is having a divide over crypto with regard to what it could facilitate for the Consensus in their favor, vs those who realize that any technology that necessitate becoming less energy efficient over time (as that's how the scarcity for it to be used as currency is maintained) is a non-starter for the long term survival of human civilization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T14:49:00-08:00","id":1473698,"title":"","content":"That, and the Syndicate is involved in Cryto in their grey area doings. Which also probably means they have ItX on their payroll to keep an eye on things, so consider cryptoshenanigans that can cause a 'market correction' to be on the radar.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...until some yahoo Syndicate Manager cause it themselves.<br /> That said, I'm sure a VA could become quite rich by hiding among the others that manage it. They just have to do it with more subtle nudges in their favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T10:15:58-08:00","id":1473757,"title":"","content":"Years ago I had a concept for a Syndicate Rep who came up with Primecoin (not the name it would be given in public), a cryptocurrency backed up against the value and the anti-magickal properties of Primium. Essentially Primecoin exists as a theoretical currency which is immune to the predations of reality deviants, and since its value is backed up by that of Primium (in theory you could trade a certain number of Primecoin for a quantity of Primium, if you know what that is and where to trade it in) it would maintain its value among Syndicate reps. A meta-currency for those who play with billions like they were nothing.<br /> <br /> The concept being laughed out of a Syndicate board meeting is what led to him becoming such a washed up and desperate deal-maker who recruits all sorts of Deviants to get his own back at the people who laughed at his ideas, and refused to supply him with thirty tones of Primium for his blockchain experiment.<br /> <br /> &quot;You fools, don't you see? The process of destroying the gold has minted it INTO the blockchain, a whole new reality! Goldcoin is a proof of concept for Primecoin, I just need more time and funds!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T19:40:58-08:00","id":1473785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote