you live in the physical urbanized world of the mortal plane. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T06:02:29-08:00","id":1474617,"title":"","content":"In my version of the WoD almost all mages have access to at least Resources 3 if they need it, but few outside of the Syndicate openly flaunt their wealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T06:07:20-08:00","id":1474619,"title":"","content":"I don't know; the Hermetics seem like they'd have no problem flaunting their wealth. And what makes the Syndicate unique isn't so much that they flaunt it as that they Focus on it: other factions that deal with money magick do so in the context of something else, whereas the Syndicate puts it at the core of its beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T14:30:58-08:00","id":1474646,"title":"","content":"It's also important to remember that &quot;wealth&quot; and &quot;money&quot; aren't actually the same thing. Money is, of course, a very useful way to get wealth, but there are other methods. The reason why you &quot;flaunt wealth&quot; as a concept is you're showing of things that would either cost far more money than your socioeconomic peers would have, or you're showing off something that has value due to rarity such that even with obscene amounts of money, it's not just something you can buy. Fine art is such a common object for flaunting because it hits both having a large price tag, and there is generally only one acknowledged original copy so only one person gets to own it.<br /> <br /> I think one of the ways that the Syndicate is different is that the Syndicate actually values money, where most other money magic happy mages actually value wealth. To your rich bastard Hermetic, money is just a means to an end of acquiring wealth, just like it is for most humans. Most people don't care about money because they want stacks of coins and bills (at least not circulating ones) to stare at. They want money because it gives them access to goods, services, and - with enough money - significant wealth. To the Syndicate wealth is subservient to money. Wealth is still important (stock markets aren't something they ignore), but only as part of the feedback mechanisms that define the value of money. Wealth that isn't generating money is just a fancy bauble. It might still have some value as social currency or artistic merit, but until you sell it? It's just sitting there. Wealth that generates money, is means to the end of having power because money is what actually forms the basis for human civilization: the ability to buy and trade with abstract units of value.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T01:52:26-08:00","id":1474713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439526-so-are-virtual-adepts-automatically-rich-in-the-age-of-bitcoin#post1439526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, with their computers they can just pour out a fortune in Bitcoin. They could even switch to various altcoins like Cardano and Dogecoin whenever flooding the market causes one coin to crash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking from a game balance point of view, are you saying that Virtual Adepts should start the game with a higher Resources rating for free? Because there's a good reason why the game design doesn't have a background called Money/Cash/Bitcoin/whatever. One reason resources are abstract is so that you can't simply say 'I cast a spell to give me Resources 5'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T03:09:20-08:00","id":1474716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1439526-so-are-virtual-adepts-automatically-rich-in-the-age-of-bitcoin?p=1474646#post1474646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the ways that the Syndicate is different is that the Syndicate actually values money, where most other money magic happy mages actually value wealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmh, that's not quite how I read Syndicate Revised.<br /> If you consider the Syndicate's focus on 'Value', money itself actually is not that important to them - it is a tool for them to use for the transmission of value from one to another, and money itself is actually labeled by them clinically as one of their &quot;temporal resources&quot; in the book.<br /> <br /> In a way the Syndicate is neither interested in Wealth (Though it's a side-effect / result of what they do), nor Money (It's merely one of the tools they use to do what they do), but the creation of value, the fulfillment of desires, and the solving of needs. It's pretty much what their whole Hypereconomics and concept of Primal Energy are about. Granted, money is a 'symbol' of what they do, and it certainly is important, given that it drives the whole economy - but to a proper Syndicate memnber, actually piling up money is per se not important.<br /> <br /> Now, of course everybody knows that the Syndicate Mages are some of the richest around - but I dare say that those whose *goal* is to just make money and get rich are exactly those that either don't make it far in the Syndicate as they miss its point, or are clever and corrupt enough to hide that goal beneath a veneer of other enlightened goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-15-2022, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T03:38:25-08:00","id":1474718,"title":"","content":"I think you missed the last sentence of that paragraph: &quot; Wealth that generates money, is means to the end of having power because money is what actually forms the basis for human civilization: the ability to buy and trade with abstract units of value.&quot;<br /> <br /> Value is, of course the (quint)essential goal of the Syndicates efforts. Money is just a tool, but tools are very important to mages when it's part of how they do their magic. The idea that the Syndicate values money instead of wealth isn't that they want to horde money as some precious thing to have as much of as possible. They value money because of its function as a key part of economic productivity that results in Value (what they're really after).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}